<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What lighting is recommended for warehouse and logistics facilities?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">The best lighting for warehouses balances high-bay efficiency, instant-on performance at cold temperatures, and DLC-rebate eligibility. We recommend LED high-bays with integrated occupancy sensors to maximize energy savings in racking aisles.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">Are there DLC rebates for warehouse lighting retrofits?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Yes, many utility programs offer significant rebates for warehouse retrofits, especially when upgrading to DLC Premium listed high-bays combined with networked lighting controls (NLC).</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What CCT and lumen levels are required for warehouse aisles?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Warehouses typically require 4000K or 5000K color temperatures for optimal visibility and safety. Lumen requirements vary by ceiling height, but 40-foot racking aisles often need 20,000 to 30,000+ lumen fixtures with narrow optics.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What controls do warehouse facilities need?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Warehouses benefit most from aisle-level occupancy sensing and daylight harvesting. Using Bluetooth mesh or PIR sensors allows fixtures to dim to 10% when aisles are empty, slashing energy costs.</p>
</article>
